---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Grigori Guitchounts: neuroscientist, AI researcher at Flagship Pioneering, and science writer.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" style="padding-top:3rem">
      <div class="prose">
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p>
          I was born in Moscow and moved to the United States when I was ten. I am a neuroscientist
          by training and now work on artificial intelligence, mostly on the question of how the
          internal states of large neural networks give rise to what they do.
        </p>
        <p>
          I studied at Boston University and spent two years as a technician in
          <a href="https://www.gardnerlab.org">Tim Gardner's</a> lab, building carbon-fiber electrode
          arrays for recording from single neurons in singing zebra finches over months. I received my PhD in
          Neuroscience from Harvard in 2020, working with David Cox on how three-dimensional head
          movement shapes activity in the visual cortex of freely moving rats, and did postdoctoral
          work at Harvard Medical School with Sandeep Robert Datta.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since 2022 I have been at <a href={site.links.flagship}>Flagship Pioneering</a>, where I am a
          Senior Principal Scientist on the Pioneering Intelligence team. My research there applies ideas
          from systems neuroscience, dynamical systems and population geometry in particular, to the
          internals of transformers and biological foundation models. I am also a co-founder of a
          Flagship company, still in stealth, focused on AI and mental health. With Jesseba Fernando I write
          <a href={site.links.substack}>Of Two Minds</a>, a newsletter about natural and artificial brains.
        </p>
        <p>
          My essays and reporting have appeared in <a href="https://www.noemamag.com">Noema</a>, <a href={site.links.nautilus}>Nautilus</a>, and
          <a href="https://undark.org">Undark</a>, on animal research, the epistemics of neuroscience,
          psychedelics, open-access publishing, and the history of Soviet science.
        </p>
        <p class="small">
          <i>Guitchounts</i> is pronounced <i>gee-chunz</i>: <i>gee</i> like geese, <i>chunz</i> like you just sneezed.
        </p>
        <h3 style="margin-top:2.5rem">Contact</h3>
        <ul class="small">
          <li><a href={site.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href={site.links.github}>GitHub</a></li>
          <li><a href={site.links.scholar}>Google Scholar</a></li>
          <li><a href={site.links.substack}>Of Two Minds on Substack</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="figure">
        <img src="/images/gg.jpg" alt="Portrait of Grigori Guitchounts" width="675" height="900" />
        <figcaption><b>Fig. 2.</b> The author, again.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
